# .env.example: the list of environment variables this project needs.
# This file IS committed. It holds NAMES and placeholders, never real values.
#
# To run the project:
#   1. Copy this file to .env       (cp .env.example .env)
#   2. Put the real values in .env  (.env is in .gitignore and is never committed)
#   3. In production, set the same names in your host's secret settings.
#
# Variables starting with NEXT_PUBLIC_, VITE_, EXPO_PUBLIC_, PUBLIC_ or
# REACT_APP_ are copied into the browser, where anyone can read them.
# Never give a secret one of those names.

# Example (replace with your own):
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DB
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
